  "runtime_image_archive_sha256": "d9a4bfc6c703f05282ffb74a7b40ac4b7475046af3b92b70419ca28eeee78ebb",
  "environment": "Linux AMD64 with R 4.4.2 and samtools 1.21 from the 0.9.9 engine. The planner received four CPUs and 3,905 MiB with the small Apple Silicon guest flag. The ordinary-profile comparison used the same budget with the flag off. Each run used a four-CPU affinity set recorded with the measurement. The nine-BAM DNP-only repeat used the same four CPUs on both revisions. This environment had no Lima, Rosetta or enforced 3,905 MiB cgroup limit.",
  "timing": "The final reader uses the original parser for a single BAM. Multi-sample timing pairs were run just before this singleton guard and follow the same multi-sample path. Each before/after pair ran once. Durations are elapsed seconds from native workflow and DNP step records with performance diagnostics. The read and compute durations are summed over workers. DNP-only repetitions exclude SNP execution.",
  "input": "The timing workload is the distributed synthetic-trio timing.bam, repeated at distinct paths with separate sample IDs. Both panels have 128 loci on four contigs, each with 600 REF and 400 ALT reads. The nine-distinct sample test uses three sites with 50 REF reads and respectively 1, 6, 11, 16, 21, 26, 31, 36 and 41 ALT reads per sample. The ordinary-profile test uses the distributed heterogeneous trio.",
  "timing_bam_sha256": "53b921513716cc9d5e1774e374f0d2a415daa8c5af20eb342ff318396faf214a",
  "memory": "The observer sampled summed proportional set size of the process tree approximately every half second during the DNP R coordinator lifetime. A null value indicates that the observer had no reliable measurement. An individual sample may miss transient peaks.",
  "outputs": "The individual call tables and aggregate genotype summaries were compared byte for byte. Positions and counts were independently checked against expected results. All recorded comparisons passed.",
